WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.440
Hey WalletHubbers! Today we’re talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.920
whether you can cancel your&nbsp;
car insurance at any time.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.720
The short answer is yes. You will&nbsp;
even receive a partial refund&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:25.440
if you pay your premium in advance and&nbsp;
cancel before the end of your policy term.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.440
However, some car insurance companies may charge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.880
a fee for canceling your policy&nbsp;
before the end of the policy term.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.000
There are generally two types of fees car&nbsp;
insurance companies charge for cancellation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.400
flat fees and short-rate fees.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:46.160
Flat fees are fixed charges that do not change&nbsp;
based on how much of the policy term is left.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.600
On the other hand, short-rate fees are a&nbsp;
penalty for early cancellation that allow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:57.840
insurance companies to keep more of your premium,&nbsp;
above what would be withheld on a pro-rated basis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.480
Short-rate fees get less expensive the&nbsp;
further into the policy term you are.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.120
Before canceling your car insurance,&nbsp;
you need to gather some information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.880
including your Social Security&nbsp;
number, car insurance policy number,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.640
driver’s license number, and&nbsp;
preferred cancellation date.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:21.680
Lastly, be sure that you have a new insurance&nbsp;
policy set up to overlap with your current one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.960
so you can avoid a lapse in coverage.&nbsp;
Just note that some insurers require&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:32.000
30-days’ notice before cancellation, so you&nbsp;
don’t want to get a new policy too early.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.400
Now that you know a bit more&nbsp;
about canceling car insurance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.040
you’re ready to start the&nbsp;
transition to a new insurer.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:52.320
To check out WalletHub’s guide to switching car&nbsp;
insurance companies, just click the button here.

